# Tyche environment template.
#
# Copy this file to $TYCHE_HOME/.env (your PRIVATE workspace, not this repo) and fill
# it in. Never commit the real file and never paste its values into logs, issues or
# chats. Variables are read in the phase noted beside them; until then they are ignored.
#
# Format (docs/adr/0040): one KEY=value per line; the value may be in matching quotes;
# no `export`, no ${VAR}, no comment after a value. Only the keys below are allowed, so
# a misspelt key is an error. A variable set in your shell wins over this file.

# Where your private workspace lives: config, data, database, logs, reports, proposals.
# Keep it outside this repository, and not under ~/Public (shared on the local network
# when File Sharing is on), ~/Desktop or ~/Documents (which macOS can sync to iCloud).
# See docs/adr/0008.
TYCHE_HOME=~/tyche-workspace

# --- Notifications (Phase 2) ---------------------------------------------------
# Discord channel webhook URL: https://discord.com/api/webhooks/<id>/<token>.
# Anyone holding this URL can post to the channel. Check it with `tyche notify test`.
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=

# --- Interactive Brokers (Phase 2) ---------------------------------------------
# Connection to a locally running IB Gateway, logged in to the PAPER account.
# The port and account-id conventions will be confirmed against IBKR's current docs
# in Phase 2 and documented in the user guide; these names are placeholders until then.
IBKR_HOST=127.0.0.1
IBKR_PORT=
IBKR_CLIENT_ID=1
# Tyche refuses to trade if the connected account does not match the one configured
# for the current mode.
IBKR_ACCOUNT_ID=

# There is deliberately no TYCHE_MODE=live switch in this file. Going live is a
# manual, documented procedure that only Pablo performs. See docs/adr/0013.
